// Typechecks the test suite in `scripts/` — which nothing did until now.
//
// `tsconfig.json` includes only `src`, so `pnpm typecheck` never looked at
// verify.ts: the single file that asserts how the whole model behaves was the
// single file the compiler ignored. It had already drifted into duplicate
// imports and a dead comparison, neither of which failed anything, because
// tsx runs what tsc would have rejected.
//
// A separate config rather than adding "scripts" to the main include: these
// are a Node program and the app is browser code. Sharing one config means
// `types: ["node"]` applies to `src` too, which quietly changes what globals
// like `setTimeout` resolve to in application code. Keeping the two type
// environments apart is the point, so the suite gets its own.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "types": ["node"],
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["scripts"]
}
